REPLACE_ME_WITH_A_LONG_RANDOM_PASSPHRASE

# Copy to secrets/restic-password, replacing the line above with a real
# passphrase and deleting these comments -- restic reads the whole file, so
# anything left here becomes part of the password.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 48
#
# KEEP A COPY SOMEWHERE ELSE. A password manager, or on paper. This file gets
# backed up into the very repository it unlocks, which is circular and no help
# at all in the situation where you need it. Lose this passphrase and every
# snapshot is unrecoverable -- there is no reset, no escrow, and Yandex cannot
# help because they only ever held encrypted blobs.
#
# Repository: rclone:yandex:restic/home
